      },
      "message": "feat(tools)!: .camtools version 8 carries tool components and stacks\n\nA tool built from tool components now rides its .camtools definition\nwith its stack (`assembly`), and the file holds the rows the stacks\nname as a top-level `components` array, in the project's one component\nwire form. Such a file says version 8 (ASSEMBLY_VERSION); a library\nwithout a stack keeps its older number and bytes.\n\nThe reader is strict: the table is read whole (each row built again\nand refused by its id), each stack must name rows of the table and\nresolve, a row that no stack names is refused, and a pre-8 file that\nstates a table or a stack is refused. ImportTools lands the rows and\nthe tools in its one undo step. A document row of the same id is\nreused when its content is the same and refuses the import by the id\nwhen it differs (docs/decisions/3645-camtools-v8.md). The two older\nsuites that named version 8 as the first unknown number now name 9.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a .camtools file with assembled tools is version 8;\nbuilds that read version 7 and older refuse it.\n\nFixes #3645\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
